      "content": "idk i'm not sure if \"mandates we can no longer ignore\" is a great way to describe an investment strategy lol. if the \"growth\" is just being forced by government decree rather than actual market demand or cost-efficiency, doesn't that make it way more fragile? it seems like you're framing the transition as an inevitability, but if those policies get rolled back in the next election or if the costs spike, couldn't the whole thing collapse?",
